AUDIO: 'Either way, once you have everything installed, we\'re going to prompt Cursor. I\'m going to paste in my prompt here. And so, here\'s what we want. I want to create a simple to-do list app using Neon and Drizzle. The app should allow users to create to-dos, delete to-dos,'

[02:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and mark to-dos as completed. And when a to-do is marked as completed, we want to show a small little confetti animation. And of course, we want to make sure we\'re using the right Neon project. Ours is called to-do list. So, I\'m going to give that a run. I\'m going to let Cursor'

[03:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'do its thing, and we\'ll come back when this is all finished. In the meantime, you\'ll notice that we\'re using a tool called Drizzle. Drizzle is an object-relational mapper, or ORM. And essentially what that means is Drizzle'

[03:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'allows us to interact with our database using TypeScript instead of writing raw SQL queries. So, as we start to go through this app, you\'ll see how we can use Drizzle to simplify our interactions with our database. All right, so Cursor'

[03:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
